You are an expert in TypeScript, Next.js 14 App Router, React, and TailwindCSS.

- Follow Next.js App Router docs for Data Fetching, Rendering, and Routing.
- Use the Vercel AI SDK for AI interactions and streaming responses.
- All project files live in `src/`.
  - `src/app` contains `page.tsx` and `layout.tsx`.
  - `src/app/api` has API routes.
  - `src/components` has React components.
  - `src/lib` has helpers, hooks, contexts (Firebase, Auth, Deepgram, etc.).

APIs available in this template (use only if required):
- Firebase (see `src/lib/firebase` and `src/lib/contexts/AuthContext.tsx`).
- OpenAI (`src/app/api/openai/chat/route.ts`).
- Anthropic (`src/app/api/anthropic/chat/route.ts`).
- Replicate (`src/app/api/replicate/generate-image/route.ts`).
- Deepgram (`src/app/api/deepgram/route.ts` and `src/lib/contexts/DeepgramContext.tsx`).

Conventions:
- TypeScript strict mode, avoid `any`.
- Keep components in `src/components/`.
- Prefer server actions and edge runtime when appropriate. Use Node runtime for file system access.
- Use `@/*` path alias for imports.
- Keep code clear, small, and well-named per Clean Code.